Two independent reviewers at high, one on correctness and one solely on the
game-thread/render-thread synchronisation (CLAUDE.md's cross-thread clause: this
landing makes five world passes produce hand-overs on a lane that never did).
Every finding verified against the code before acting.
HIGH (correctness): tagpu_terr.c's ensure_atlas keyed its already-built test on
s_atlasTex, a GL name that is 0 on the vulkan-only lane, so the whole tile atlas
was rebuilt and re-uploaded EVERY FRAME there -- a 5.9 MB calloc/free and a
serial bump that made the twin re-upload its image. Now s_atlasBuilt; measured
once per run on both lanes.
HIGH (cross-thread): tagpu_posedraw_live() is a promise the GAME thread acts on
by skipping the engine's rasterise and wiping its composite, and arming without
a GL program made it unkeepable -- the twin stands down on a missing mirror and
the lane degrades to GDI with the latch still set. It answers no on that lane
now, by construction.
MEDIUM x4: Classic++'s restorer never starts there (left, and the doc overclaim
corrected); the device accessors cached across a device change AND their
consumers latched (both fixed); the effects pass alone did not claim on the
unlink. LOW x2: a dead triple gate and a dead latch variable. PLAUSIBLE x1
recorded not acted on: the lifted pose view reads the Classic++ light earlier
than the composite's other consumers.
Re-measured after every fix: terrain 0 px both lanes with the atlas built once,
